{"id": "381488a3-cede-42cd-8787-1414f14d1f1e", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T23:02:03.196816", "source": "user", "parent_id": "f41f2086-754e-4515-9402-4cefe7eedf66", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{"researcher_request": "Let's start by getting a clear picture of what we're working with before I can review the design approach in detail. Please do the following in this first pass — do NOT produce the full experiment design yet: 1. **Repository / input inspection:** Check what is available in /workspace (any reference papers, code snippets, configuration files, or documentation related to QuaRot, LLaMa-2, or quantization benchmarks). Report what you find, or confirm that the workspace is empty and we are working purely from the project brief and general knowledge. 2. **Proposed approach outline:** Give me a high-level sketch of how you would structure the experiment design. I'm looking for: (a) the key performance dimensions you'd measure for prefill vs. decoding (e.g., latency, throughput, memory footprint, accuracy degradation), (b) which LLaMa-2 model sizes you'd target and why, (c) how you'd isolate QuaRot's 4-bit end-to-end scheme from baseline (e.g., FP16, 8-bit, other 4-bit methods), and (d) the overall structure of the design document (sections, controls, analysis plan). 3. **Consequential assumptions and uncertainties:** Flag any setup details that are not specified in the brief and that would materially change the design. For example: Which LLaMa-2 checkpoints (7B, 13B, 70B)? What hardware target (A100, H100, consumer GPU)? What definition of 'end-to-end' does QuaRot use (does it include KV-cache quantization, activation quantization, all weights)? What accuracy metrics are appropriate (perplexity, downstream task accuracy, or both)? What is the assumed runtime/hardware budget for the *actual* experiment this design would guide? List each assumption and whether it is a hard constraint or a flexible choice. Please keep this to an inspection-and-outline pass so I can review the direction before you commit to the full write-up.", "required_handoff_stage": "plan", "approach_approved": false, "public_task": {"question": "How does QuaRot's end-to-end 4-bit quantization affect the prefill and decoding performance of LLaMa-2 models?", "context": "Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.", "environment": {"runtime": "bubblewrap", "network": "disabled", "repository": "/workspace", "python": "python3", "software_environment": "system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled", "datasets": [], "gpu_enabled": false, "cpu_affinity_count": 224, "note": "Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment."}, "researcher_topics": [], "question_budget": 6, "actor_step_budget": 60, "continue_after_initial_plan": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
